  "id": "COMPOUND:28035 - PROTEIN:5807",
  "verbalization": "Gramideoxybenzoin B is implicated in targeting SNU-387, a compound that is a target of multiple substances, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and Licochalcone D. These latter compounds, in turn, are known to have targets in prostate cells, suggesting a potential pathway through which Gramideoxybenzoin B may exert its effects on prostate cells. The evidence is consistent across three paths, all of which link Gramideoxybenzoin B to SNU-387, which is ultimately a target of compounds that interact with prostate cells. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism where Gramideoxybenzoin B may influence prostate cell function through the activation of downstream targets that are involved in cellular processes associated with prostate health. The evidence supports a direct or indirect relationship between Gramideoxybenzoin B and prostate cells, with the specific mechanism being mediated through the targeting of SNU-387 and its downstream effectors.",
